msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:118
msgid "Turn me off"
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:119
msgid "Oh"
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:122
msgid "You are staring. That makes me shy."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:123
msgid "I can feel you looking at me."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:124
msgid "Is there something on my face?"
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:125
msgid "Shouldn't you be building something?"
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:126
msgid "I do not get any prettier, you know."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:127
msgid "Still here. Still a small blue box."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:128
msgid "This is a lot of eye contact."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:130
msgid "Hey"
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:132
msgid "Why are you deleting that?"
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:133
msgid "It did nothing to you."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:134
msgid "Gone. I hope you meant that."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:135
msgid "That one was my favourite."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:154
msgid "The page outline, not a font size. One h1, then h2s under it — jumping to h4 because it looks smaller is what breaks the outline for screen readers and search."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:155
msgid "A block of body copy. Set the measure here, not by squeezing the column: past about 75 characters a line the eye loses its place on the way back."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:156
msgid "Fill in the alt text — it is what a screen reader reads and what shows when the file fails. A purely decorative image takes an empty alt, not a missing one."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:157
msgid "Set a poster image or the space sits blank until the file loads. Autoplay only works muted, and it spends someone's data before they have asked for it."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:158
msgid "Say what happens next, not \"Click here\". One obvious primary button per screenful — a second of equal weight makes the visitor choose instead of act."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:159
msgid "A line between sections. If the spacing already reads as a break, the line is noise; reach for it when the gap alone is not doing the work."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:160
msgid "Sometimes the honest tool. But if you are stacking spacers to push something down, the padding on the section above is the real fix."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:161
msgid "An icon beside a label reads faster than either alone. On its own it needs a title — not everyone reads the same symbol the same way."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:162
msgid "Image, heading and text as one unit. Keep the images the same shape across a row or the headings below them will not line up."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:163
msgid "A feature in three parts. The heading carries the meaning — if the icon were removed the box should still make sense."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:164
msgid "For short parallel items: features, what is included. Once a line wraps to three rows it has become body copy and wants a text block."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:165
msgid "These send people away from your page. Footer, usually — not beside the thing you want them to do."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:166
msgid "Raw markup, straight out. Nothing here is sanitised or responsive for you, so what you paste is exactly what ships."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:167
msgid "Runs another plugin's shortcode. It renders on the live page but usually not in the builder, so check the front end before calling it done."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:168
msgid "Pulls the logo from site settings, so changing it once changes it everywhere. Give it a height, not a width — logos differ in shape more than in height."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:169
msgid "The site name from settings. In a header this is usually a link home; as a page heading it competes with the real h1."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:170
msgid "Your WordPress menu. Seven items is about the limit before people stop reading and start scanning — anything more belongs in a submenu."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:171
msgid "Worth having once results are worth finding. On a small site it often just advertises that there is not much here."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:172
msgid "The title of the post being viewed. Only resolves inside a Single template; anywhere else it comes out empty."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:173
msgid "The post's own image. Set a ratio so a tall photo and a wide one do not shove the rest of the template around."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:174
msgid "The short summary. If the post has none written, WordPress cuts one mid-sentence — writing excerpts is what makes a listing read well."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:175
msgid "Date, author, category. Pick what a reader actually needs; four meta items above the first line is throat-clearing."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:176
msgid "Where the post body lands in a Single template. One per template — a second copy renders the same content twice."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:177
msgid "Who wrote it. Worth it on a multi-author site, filler on a one-person blog."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:178
msgid "Previous and next. Useful in a series, arbitrary when the posts have nothing to do with each other."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:179
msgid "The comment thread. If comments are off in Discussion settings this renders nothing, which looks like a bug but is not."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:180
msgid "The title of the archive being viewed. Only resolves in an Archive template."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:181
msgid "The category or tag description. Most sites never fill these in, so it is usually empty — write them or drop this."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:182
msgid "A list of posts with its own query. Set the count deliberately: the default is the site's, and it changes under you when someone edits Reading settings."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:183
msgid "Posts rendered through a Loop Item template, so the card is yours. Build the Loop Item first — without it there is nothing to repeat."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:184
msgid "Products in a grid. Decide what happens at three items and at thirty; a grid that looks right with nine often falls apart at four."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:185
msgid "The buy button for one product. On a variable product it needs the variation controls too, or it adds nothing."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:186
msgid "Price, with the sale price when there is one. It follows the product, so do not type the number anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:187
msgid "The product's images. Shoppers zoom — upload bigger than you display."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:188
msgid "Cart with a count. Keep it in the header on every page; a shopper who cannot find the cart does not go looking."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:189
msgid "The cart contents. Belongs on the Cart page only — anywhere else it renders someone's cart in the middle of your content."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:190
msgid "The whole checkout. Every field you add loses you orders, so ask only for what you need to ship."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:191
msgid "Browsable categories. If you have four, show them; if you have forty, this becomes a wall."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:192
msgid "Narrow by attribute. Only filter on what people shop by — size and price, usually, not everything you store."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:193
msgid "The cart in a dropdown. It needs a clear route to checkout or it is a dead end."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:194
msgid "Stars from real reviews. With two reviews it reads as thin; wait until you have some."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:195
msgid "The customer's account area. Belongs on its own page behind a login, not in your main flow."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:196
msgid "Scrolling text. Readable as a strip of logos or short phrases, unreadable for anything you expect people to take in."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:197
msgid "A person: photo, name, role. Crop every face to the same ratio or the row looks accidental."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:198
msgid "Several quotes in rotation. Most visitors see the first and nothing else, so put your strongest one there."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:199
msgid "A pulled quote. For emphasis, not for every paragraph you like — once everything is pulled out, nothing is."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:200
msgid "Opening times. Remember the holiday that makes this wrong; an out-of-date table is worse than none."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:201
msgid "Markers over an image. Touch has no hover, so on a phone each marker must be tappable."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:202
msgid "Filterable work. The filter earns its place at about a dozen items; below that it is a control nobody touches."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:203
msgid "Sign in without wp-admin. Set where it goes afterwards, or people land on a dashboard they did not want."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:204
msgid "Hides its back until hover. Nothing important goes on the back — on a phone it may never be seen."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:205
msgid "Plans side by side. Mark the one you want chosen; three undifferentiated columns leave people stuck."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:206
msgid "Only for a deadline that is real. A timer that resets on refresh gets noticed, and it costs trust you do not get back."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:207
msgid "One phrase that changes. The sentence has to read properly with every variant, including the longest."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:208
msgid "Image, heading and a button as one block. One idea and one button — a CTA with two buttons is a menu."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:209
msgid "Sharing links. Four is plenty; a row of twelve looks like hope rather than strategy."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:210
msgid "Page numbers for a list. It only does something where a query is paged, so it belongs with Posts or Loop Grid."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:211
msgid "Good for questions people scan. Bad for anything they must read — folded content is content most visitors never open."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:212
msgid "One panel that opens. For a single aside; several of these want to be an accordion so only one is open at a time."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:213
msgid "For alternatives: pick one of these. Not for a sequence — if panel two only makes sense after panel one, they want to be sections."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:214
msgid "A number that counts up on scroll. It needs a label saying what it counts, or it is a moving digit."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:215
msgid "A proportion, shown. Say what the number is out of, or the bar means nothing."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:216
msgid "A notice that needs reading. Use it rarely — two alerts on a page and people stop seeing either."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:217
msgid "A rating you type in yourself. Say where it came from; an unsourced five stars reads as decoration."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:218
msgid "One quote. A name, a role and a face make it believable — without them it reads as something you wrote."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:219
msgid "Images in rotation. Most people see the first and nothing else, so if image three matters it should not be in here."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:220
msgid "A grid of images. Set the columns per breakpoint: four across looks right on a laptop and turns into stamps on a phone."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:221
msgid "An embed that loads third-party code on every visit. If the address is the point, a static image and a link are lighter and just as useful."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:222
msgid "Every field costs you submissions. Ask for what you will actually use, and label the fields above them, not inside."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:223
msgid "A hint on hover. Touch has no hover, so nothing a visitor needs can live only in here."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:224
msgid "Built from the headings. It is only as good as the outline, so fix the headings first and this fixes itself."
msgstr ""

#: editor/mascot/class-loopkit-mascot.php:225
msgid "Shows rows from a CMS collection, one card each. Bind the image, title and link to fields once — then adding a row updates the page by itself."
msgstr ""

